cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use bitig, please cite it as below."
title: "bitig: next-generation computational stylometry"
authors:
  - family-names: "Bozdağ"
    given-names: "Fatih"
    email: "fbozdag1989@gmail.com"
type: software
license: BSD-3-Clause
url: "https://github.com/fatihbozdag/bitig"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fatihbozdag/bitig"
version: "0.3.1"
abstract: >
  bitig is a Python package and command-line tool for computational stylometry.
  It covers authorship attribution, author-group comparison and related
  Digital Humanities analyses (Delta, Zeta, dimensionality reduction,
  clustering, bootstrap consensus trees, classification), drawing on methods
  popularised by R's Stylo, and builds on spaCy and scikit-learn.
keywords:
  - stylometry
  - authorship-attribution
  - corpus-linguistics
  - digital-humanities
  - natural-language-processing
